<main id="main">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The missing manual for Change Data Capture</span>
        <h1>Read your database's <span class="accent">change log</span> like a stream.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Every insert, update, and delete &mdash; captured from the transaction log and turned into an event you can trust. Learn CDC from first principles to production, edge cases and all.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn primary" href="#modules">Start with the intro <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="#modules">Browse the series</a>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-row">
          <span class="stat"><b>24</b><span>guided modules</span></span>
          <span class="stat"><b>4</b><span>hands-on labs</span></span>
          <span class="stat"><b>0</b><span>vendor pitches</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" aria-label="Example change event emitted from a row update">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="t">stream &middot; public.customer</span></div>
        <div class="stream">
          <div class="c">-- a row changes in Postgres&hellip;</div>
          <div class="row"><span class="k">UPDATE</span> customer <span class="k">SET</span> tier=<span class="after">'pro'</span> <span class="k">WHERE</span> id=<span class="s">42</span>;</div>
          <div class="emit"><span>emits</span><span class="track"><b></b></span><span>Debezium event</span></div>
          <div class="row">{ <span class="k">"op"</span>: <span class="op-pill op-u">u&nbsp;update</span> </div>
          <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px"><span class="k">"before"</span>: { "id": <span class="s">42</span>, "tier": <span class="before">"free"</span> },</div>
          <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px"><span class="k">"after"</span>&nbsp;: { "id": <span class="s">42</span>, "tier": <span class="after">"pro"</span> },</div>
          <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px"><span class="k">"ts_ms"</span>: <span class="s">1724130512034</span>,</div>
          <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px"><span class="k">"lsn"</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;: <span class="s">"0/1A2B3C0"</span> }<span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap" style="margin-top:34px">
      <div class="pipe">
        <div class="stage"><span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">&#128738;</span><span class="lbl"><b>Source DB</b><span>WAL &middot; binlog &middot; redo</span></span></div>
        <span class="link"><b></b></span>
        <div class="stage"><span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">&#10226;</span><span class="lbl"><b>Connector</b><span>Debezium</span></span></div>
        <span class="link"><b></b></span>
        <div class="stage"><span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">&#8779;</span><span class="lbl"><b>Stream</b><span>Kafka &middot; offsets</span></span></div>
        <span class="link"><b></b></span>
        <div class="stage"><span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">&#9636;</span><span class="lbl"><b>Sink</b><span>warehouse &middot; idempotent</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MODULE CARDS -->
  <section id="modules">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <span class="offset">LSN 0/01 &mdash; THE SERIES</span>
          <h2>Follow the change from log to warehouse</h2>
          <p>A sequenced path: capture, deliver, and materialize changes &mdash; each module builds on the offset before it.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn ghost sm" href="#">All 24 modules &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <a class="card" href="#"><span class="num">0x01</span><h3>Introduction to CDC</h3><p>Log-based vs. trigger vs. query capture, and why real-time beats nightly batch.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag concept"><i></i>concept</span><span class="level">Beginner</span></div></a>
        <a class="card" href="#"><span class="num">0x04</span><h3>Snapshotting</h3><p>The consistent-read boundary, incremental snapshots, and the snapshot&rarr;stream handoff.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag pattern"><i></i>pattern</span><span class="level">Core</span></div></a>
        <a class="card" href="#"><span class="num">0x05</span><h3>Exactly-Once</h3><p>At-least-once truth, idempotent sinks, and why "effectively-once" is the honest goal.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag concept"><i></i>concept</span><span class="level">Core</span></div></a>
        <a class="card" href="#"><span class="num">0x08</span><h3>Schema Evolution</h3><p>Registry compatibility modes and the upgrade order that won't break consumers.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag concept"><i></i>concept</span><span class="level">Core</span></div></a>
        <a class="card" href="#"><span class="num">0x07</span><h3>Partitioning &amp; Ordering</h3><p>Key choice, per-key order, skew, and version-guarded idempotent writes.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag ops"><i></i>ops</span><span class="level">Advanced</span></div></a>
        <a class="card" href="#"><span class="num">0x03</span><h3>Materialization</h3><p>Upsert, delete, SCD2, and late arrivals &mdash; dedupe on log position, not <code class="inl">ts_ms</code>.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag pattern"><i></i>pattern</span><span class="level">Core</span></div></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LESSON PREVIEW -->
  <section id="lesson" style="background:var(--surface-2); border-top:1px solid var(--line); border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <span class="offset">LSN 0/04 &mdash; INSIDE A LESSON</span>
          <h2>Every module is a working surface</h2>
          <p>Readiness trackers, runnable snippets, honest caveats, and a check for understanding &mdash; not a wall of prose.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lesson">
        <div class="stack">
          <div class="tile">
            <h3>Snapshotting readiness</h3>
            <div class="sub">Track how close each checklist is to production-ready.</div>
            <div class="score-row done"><span class="check done" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span><span>Pick a consistent-read boundary</span></div>
            <div class="score-row done"><span class="check done" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span><span>Chunk large tables, bound lock time</span></div>
            <div class="score-row"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Verify the snapshot &rarr; stream watermark handoff</span></div>
            <div class="meter" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="66" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"><b></b></div>
            <div class="meter-lbl"><span>readiness</span><span>2 / 3 &middot; 66%</span></div>
          </div>
          <details class="errata">
            <summary><span class="badge" aria-hidden="true">!</span> Known errata for this page (1)</summary>
            <p><b>Corrected:</b> dedup ordering uses the source log position (LSN/SCN) as the primary sort, with <code class="inl">ts_ms</code> only as a tie-break &mdash; it isn't unique per key.</p>
          </details>
          <table class="ops" aria-label="CDC operation codes">
            <thead><tr><th>op</th><th>means</th><th>carries</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><span class="opcode c">c</span></td><td>create / insert</td><td><code class="inl">after</code> only</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="opcode u">u</span></td><td>update</td><td><code class="inl">before</code> + <code class="inl">after</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="opcode d">d</span></td><td>delete</td><td><code class="inl">before</code> + tombstone</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <div class="panel">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="t">bash &middot; verify the stream</span></div>
            <div class="stream" style="font-size:.79rem">
              <div class="c"># consume the change topic</div>
              <div class="row"><span class="k">kafka-console-consumer</span> \</div>
              <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px">--bootstrap-server <span class="s">kafka:29092</span> \</div>
              <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px">--topic <span class="s">server1.public.customer</span> \</div>
              <div class="row" style="padding-left:14px">--from-beginning --max-messages <span class="s">1</span></div>
              <div class="c" style="margin-top:8px">&rarr; { "op":"c", "after":{ "id":88, "tier":"free" } }</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="callout info"><span class="ic">i</span><span><b>Offsets are crown jewels.</b> Source-connector progress lives in <code class="inl">connect-offsets</code> &mdash; not <code class="inl">__consumer_offsets</code>. Back it up before any replay.</span></div>
          <div class="callout warn"><span class="ic">!</span><span><b>Snapshots race the stream.</b> Without a watermark, the initial load and live changes can interleave and lose an update. Fence the handoff.</span></div>
          <div class="quiz">
            <div class="q">A relay crashes after publishing an outbox event but before committing its offset. What does the sink see?</div>
            <div class="opt correct"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>A duplicate &mdash; delivery is at-least-once, so dedupe downstream</div>
            <div class="opt"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span>Nothing &mdash; the event is lost</div>
            <div class="opt"><span class="mk" aria-hidden="true"></span>Exactly one &mdash; the outbox guarantees it</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COMPONENT LIBRARY + TOKENS + TYPE -->
  <section id="library">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <span class="offset">LSN 0/0F &mdash; THE SYSTEM</span>
          <h2>Tokens, type, and every primitive</h2>
